Changes with the nginx-autocert-module            unreleased

    *) CI standardisation against nginx-skeleton-module. All CI material moved
       under ci/, and ci.yml became the single pull_request entry point: the
       other workflows are workflow_call members, so a PR asks for one run
       rather than several independent ones. Members keep their push: and
       schedule: triggers for direct coverage of master.

    *) Ported the ci/linter framework and wired lint.yml into the suite: the
       same lint-*.sh checkers run in the pre-commit hook and on the PR, so
       local green predicts remote green instead of merely correlating with
       it. The blocking set (LINT_ONLY) is a deliberate subset; a checker
       joins it in the same change that makes it green, so the gate only
       ratchets forward.

    *) Added ci/linter/lint-python.sh. ci/linter/workflow_policy.py implements
       the rule for five of the eleven checkers and had no checker of its own.
       Rules are selected explicitly because ruff's default set omits F401 and
       E402 -- a stray unused import passed a bare `ruff check`.

    *) Added ci/tools/ci-build.sh as the single chokepoint for building nginx
       plus the module, and adopted it in codeql.yml, security-scanners.yml
       and ci-deep.yml.

    *) Added a coverage build profile and ci/tools/coverage.sh, and verified
       the coverage filter actually moves rather than reporting a constant.

    *) Added a fuzz target for the base64url decode wrapper, a drift gate
       holding fuzz.dict against the parser's literals, and a replay of every
       past crash on each PR. fuzzing.yml had become orphaned from the merge
       path and was reconnected; reconnecting it exposed and fixed a stale
       corpus path.

    *) Added an ASan/UBSan soak workflow (asan.yml) on a weekly schedule, and
       fixed the two non-defects that had kept it red since it was written.
       The soak now detects a sanitizer report wherever it lands: a
       sanitizer's log_path is not a contract, and GCC's UBSan wrote its
       report into nginx's error.log rather than the configured path.

    *) Added a sync-stamp gate over the .github/ files shared with the
       skeleton, so an adopter can diff two repos and see exactly what
       drifted.

    *) Added workflow-policy checks for runner selection, port bands, trigger
       cadence and secret declarations, each with fixture trees that must go
       red.

    *) Wired ccache into the nginx configure step. It had been installed and
       configured but was never reaching the compiler, so the cache recorded
       no hits at all.

    *) Fixed a NULL-log segfault reached through the crypto unit tests, and
       closed mutation-testing gaps at the length, depth and overflow
       boundaries. A year-9999 boundary assertion compared two implementations
       that both return (time_t) -1 on a narrow time_t, so it could not fail;
       it now requires a representable reference.

    *) Scoped e2e container reaping by GITHUB_RUN_ID so concurrent jobs cannot
       kill each other's containers, and derived e2e port bands from the run
       ID with the ceiling verified before anything binds.

    *) CONTRIBUTING.md now tells a contributor to enable the pre-commit hook,
       which is what makes the local and remote gates agree.


Changes with the nginx-autocert-module 1.2.0                     11 Jul 2026

    *) See the git history and the GitHub release notes for v1.2.0 and
       earlier. This file starts at the CI standardisation above; it was not
       maintained for the releases that precede it.
